WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.128
Minutes matter.

00:00:01.128 --> 00:00:13.680
Brain cells begin to die within about four to six minutes after cardiac arrest, and irreversible injury may begin at roughly four minutes without restored circulation.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:23.452
The supplied manuals report survival near 90% with immediate reversal, around 40–50% at six minutes and about 10% by nine minutes.
